# A CLI deploy (`vercel --prod`) uploads the working directory and reads only
# this file — not .gitignore. Without it the local .env, which exists on a
# developer machine and nowhere else, is shipped into the deployment, where it
# is both unnecessary (the platform injects its own environment) and a copy of
# development secrets sitting in a production bundle.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Local-only, and large.
.next
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
